ents bishop d7 getting ready to  castle on the king side knights here to  f3 preparing the way if it wants to  bring his bishop here to  c4 b5 even check uh his opponent and  then castle on the king side kes on the  king side for black and here's where  things get interesting we see pawn two  h4  i don't think anyone was expecting this  this is not a  a book line by any means uh this is a  novel move by cardiacan and just saying  yeah uh  i i can still castle on the king's side  but i'm gonna be pretty aggressive here  and start to push up on the kingside  with my pawn h4 so we see pawn takes on  d4  pawn recaptures knight to c6 so just  development move attacking the center  and then pawn to h5 so  wow completely all in on the strategy to  attack and now doesn't even look like  white's looking to castle on the king  side which is somewhat odd it does have  a strong attack center control here  usually we're going to see white  castling have some sort of protection  and just milk his advantage in the  center of the board that's not what  we're seeing at all white's going on the  complete offensive mode here not just in  the center but on the king side  pawn to f5 uh so  vladimir saying yeah i need to do  something and counter it to actually  plays pawn to f5 after the pawn takes  queen down here a5 check bishop d2 not  too many great options as far as how to  defend this so bishop to d2 queen over  here to f5 uh bishop to c3 defending  this pawn here on d4 then pawn to h6 had  different options could have played  queen to e4 if he wanted to stay  aggressive but instead plays pawn to h6  now bishop to d3 attacking the queen  queen comes down here to a g4 attacking  the pawn here on g2 king to f1 so now  signaling for sure there's no way to  castle now does want to protect this  pawn here on g2  punt e5 saying you want to exchange  white says no trade skis today my friend  i'm going to have a pass pawn here that  you're going to have to deal with the  rest of the game 